{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.tau_leptonic_universality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tau_leptonic_universality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tau_leptonic_universality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tau_leptonic_universality","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L102-L123","doc":"**Tau leptonic universality** ([`prop:tau-leptonic-universality`]).\n\nIn the factorised model, the ratio of leptonic branching\nfractions equals the pure phase-space ratio:\n\n  `BR(τ → e) / BR(τ → μ) = f(m_e²/m_τ²) / f(m_μ²/m_τ²)`.\n\nStated against an abstract `TauLeptonicContext`; the matrix\nelement universality\n`|M_e|² = |M_μ|² = |tr_Markov(T_{3,5})|²` is recorded in the\n`phaseSpace`-only RHS. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:tau-leptonic-universality","label":"prop:tau-leptonic-universality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/tau-leptonic-universality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ_factored","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Factorisation for `τ → μ` — **same** `weakVertexTraceSq` (universality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_e_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_e_factored","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Factorisation for `τ → e`: universal matrix element × phase space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.weakVertexTraceSq_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.weakVertexTraceSq_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The universal matrix element is non-zero (the weak vertex is a\nnon-trivial mediator), so it cancels in the branching ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.weakVertexTraceSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.weakVertexTraceSq","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The **universal** squared weak matrix element\n`|𝓜|² = |tr_Markov(T_{3,5})|²` (real evaluation at `q₀`), shared by\nboth leptonic channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L89-L89","doc":"BR_μ ≠ 0 so the ratio is well-defined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_τ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_τ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_μ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_μ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_e_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_e_pos","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Positivity of masses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_μ","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Branching fraction `BR(τ → μ ν̄_μ ν_τ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.BR_e","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Branching fraction `BR(τ → e ν̄_e ν_τ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_τ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_τ","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Tau rest mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_μ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_μ","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Muon rest mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.m_e","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Electron rest mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauLeptonicContext","kind":"class","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L55-L100","doc":"Abstract context for the tau-leptonic-universality claim.\n\nThe **factorisation hypotheses** `BR_ℓ_factored` encode the physical\ncontent of the manuscript: each leptonic branching fraction factors as a\n*universal* squared matrix element times the daughter-dependent\nphase-space factor,\n\n  `BR(τ → ℓ) = |𝓜|² · f((m_ℓ / m_τ)²)`,\n\nwith the **same** `weakVertexTraceSq = |tr_Markov(T_{3,5})|²` for both\nchannels — this shared value is exactly the universality\n`|𝓜_e|² = |𝓜_μ|² = |tr_Markov((σ₀σ₁)⁵)|²`.  The Markov trace of the\nweak vertex is a property of the vertex alone (a class function on\n`H_3(q)`; cf. `QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.character_append_comm` — the\ntrace is invariant under the braid word's cyclic structure), so it does\nnot depend on the daughter lepton.  Its archimedean (real) evaluation at\nthe substrate `q₀` is the scalar `weakVertexTraceSq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L48-L53","doc":"Boundary value: `f(1) = 0` (degenerate daughter mass).\n\n`f(1) = 1 − 8 + 8 − 1 − 12·1·log 1 = 0 − 12·0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L38-L46","doc":"Boundary value: `f(0) = 1` (massless-daughter limit).\n\nStrictly speaking `phaseSpace` evaluates to `1 - 0 - 0 - 0 - 12·0·log 0`\nat `x = 0`; the `12 x² · log x` term has limit 0 as `x → 0⁺`, and\n`Real.log 0 = 0` by Mathlib convention, so the formula evaluates\nto `1` at `x = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.phaseSpace","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/tau_leptonic_universality.lean#L33-L36","doc":"The leptonic-decay phase-space factor `f(x) = 1 − 8x + 8x³ − x⁴\n− 12 x² ln x`, defined for `x > 0` (the `ln x` is `Real.log`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}